  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.52",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $L$ be a finite non-abelian simple group, and let $D$ be a conjugacy class of involutions in $L$. Consider the complete graph $\\Gamma$ with vertex set $D$. Define an equivalence relation $\\sim$ (graph coloring) on the set of edges as follows: $(a,b)\\sim(c,d)$ if and only if $|ab|=|cd|$. An automorphism of the coloured graph $\\Gamma$ is a permutation $\\tau\\in S_D$ such that $(a,b)\\sim(a^\\tau,b^\\tau)$ for every edge $(a,b)$. Is it true that the automorphism group of $\\Gamma$ is a subgroup of $\\operatorname{Aut}(L)$?",
